BT /F1 16.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 800.00 Td (Chat backend - how to run) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 776.00 Td (Users, chats, and membership live in PostgreSQL. Messages, read receipts, and last-seen) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 762.00 Td (pointers live in Firestore. The API listens on port 3000. There is no web page.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 745.00 Td (Redis is optional. It holds unread counts and the send rate limit. BullMQ uses it only after a) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 731.00 Td (message is already saved. If Redis is not running, every required chat API still succeeds.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 717.00 Td (Unread counts stay at 0 and the rate limit is skipped.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 700.00 Td (There is no WebSocket. A client sees a new message by calling GET /chat/:chatId/messages) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 686.00 Td (again.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 663.00 Td (What each part does) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 643.00 Td (PostgreSQL \(required\): users, chats, members, last-message preview, and the message sequence.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 626.00 Td (Firestore \(required\): message text, timestamp, read receipts, and last seen. Locally this is) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 612.00 Td (the Firestore emulator. The API code is the same code that talks to a real Firebase project.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 598.00 Td (Remove FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST and set GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS to use a real project.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 581.00 Td (Redis \(optional\): unread counts, send rate limit, and the BullMQ queue.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 564.00 Td (Docker \(optional\): one command that starts PostgreSQL, Redis, the Firestore emulator, and the) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 550.00 Td (API. Java is installed inside the Firestore image. The host machine does not need Java, Node,) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 536.00 Td (or a local database.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 519.00 Td (This repository does not contain live chat data. The first run creates empty tables and an) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 505.00 Td (empty emulator. Data appears when the APIs are called.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 482.00 Td (Option 1 - Docker, one command) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 462.00 Td (This is the path to use. It does not need Java on the computer, and it does not bind) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 448.00 Td (PostgreSQL \(5432\) or Redis \(6379\), so a database already running on the machine does not stop) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 434.00 Td (it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 417.00 Td (Install Docker, then from the project folder:) Tj ET
0.9608 0.9608 0.9608 rg 45 377.00 505.00 25.00 re f
BT /F3 9.50 Tf 0 g 48.00 386.00 Td (docker compose up --build) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 363.00 Td (That starts PostgreSQL, Redis, the Firestore emulator, and the API. Migrations run on startup.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 349.00 Td (The API is at http://localhost:3000.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 332.00 Td (Stop it with:) Tj ET
0.9608 0.9608 0.9608 rg 45 292.00 505.00 25.00 re f
BT /F3 9.50 Tf 0 g 48.00 301.00 Td (docker compose down) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 278.00 Td (Only two host ports are used: 3000 \(API\) and 8080 \(Firestore emulator\). Those two need to be) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 264.00 Td (free. PostgreSQL and Redis stay inside Docker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 241.00 Td (Option 2 - commands, no Docker) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 221.00 Td (Install Node.js 20 or newer, PostgreSQL 16, and Java 21. Java is only for the Firestore) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 207.00 Td (emulator. npm run emulators fails with "Unable to locate a Java Runtime" when Java 21 is) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 193.00 Td (missing. Docker does not have this requirement. Redis is optional.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.00 Tf 0 g 48.00 176.00 Td (Create the database once, as a PostgreSQL superuser:) Tj ET
